description: Prefer the smallest proven solution and one owner for each concept
alwaysApply: true
---

# Simplicity

- Search the repository before adding a second implementation of an existing concept.
- Prefer a maintained popular dependency for general-purpose problems, after checking its license, maintenance, and failure mode.
- Build only what the accepted behavior needs now. Avoid infrastructure, flags, abstractions, and compatibility paths without a current caller and a removal condition.
- Keep one source of truth for each rule, calculation, format, or state transition.
- Avoid unrelated refactors and formatting churn.
